[size=5][b]voshond's QuickSelect[/b][/size]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]

OpenMW 0.51 or newer is required.

[size=4][b]Description[/b][/size]

voshond's QuickSelect is a PC-first fork of ZackHasaCat's [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/54587]Quickselect[/url] for OpenMW. It replaces the vanilla quick-item workflow with three directly addressable, customisable hotbars for items, spells, and enchanted items.

[b]Before enabling the mod:[/b] unbind the vanilla quick-item keys so they do not conflict with QuickSelect.

[size=3][b]Highlights[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Thirty direct hotkeys:[/b] [b]1-0[/b] activate the first bar, [b]Shift[/b]/Mouse 4 + [b]1-0[/b] activate the second, and [b]Ctrl[/b]/Mouse 5 + [b]1-0[/b] activate the third. [b]-[/b] and [b]=[/b] can also change the active bar.[/*]
[*][b]Searchable assignment menus:[/b] bind inventory items, spells, and enchanted items from a mouse-friendly picker with tooltips and scrolling.[/*]
[*][b]Correct individual-item handling:[/b] assignments retain the exact item you selected, so same-record weapons or enchanted items with different condition or charge are not confused with one another.[/*]
[*][b]Useful at-a-glance information:[/b] configurable slot labels, stack counts, enchantment charges (including current/max and low-charge colours), equipped indicators, and remaining uses for equipped probes, lockpicks, and repair tools.[/*]
[*][b]Per-type low-stock warnings:[/b] optional threshold colours for potions, repair tools, probes, lockpicks, and ammunition.[/*]
[*][b]Configurable presentation:[/b] choose zero to three visible bars (zero hides the HUD while hotkeys still work), top or bottom placement, icon size, horizontal and vertical spacing, text styling, and optional auto-fading after inactivity. An optional active-hotbar-only mode keeps the HUD to one fixed row and temporarily replaces it with Hotbar 2 or 3 while its modifier is held.[/*]
[/list]

[size=3][b]PC-first behaviour[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Bars are directly addressable rather than treated as a single bar you must switch through first.[/*]
[*]Pressing a selected spell or enchanted item toggles its spell stance; choosing another spell keeps that stance ready.[/*]
[*]Pressing an equipped weapon, lockpick, probe, or light readies/switches it as appropriate. The optional [b]Auto-Unequip Sheathed Weapons[/b] setting controls whether sheathing also unequips weapons, lockpicks, and probes.[/*]
[*]Armor, clothing, and accessories can optionally be toggled off with their assigned key.[/*]
[*]Controller input remains available where OpenMW exposes it, but the mod is designed and supported primarily for keyboard-and-mouse play.[/*]
[/list]

[size=3][b]Differences from the original QuickSelect[/b][/size]

This fork deliberately does not carry forward the original persistent-mode toggle, hotbar-preview model, pause-while-selecting option, or keyboard arrow-key navigation. Visibility is controlled directly by the number of shown bars and the optional fading setting; slot numbers are configurable rather than permanently forced on.

[size=4][b]Credits[/b][/size]

Author: voshond
Original author of QuickSelect: ZackHasaCat

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Download [b]voshondsQuickSelect-vX.X.X.zip[/b] and extract its contents into an OpenMW data directory.[/*]
[*]Add [b]voshondsQuickSelect.omwscripts[/b] to your OpenMW Launcher content list.[/*]
[*]Launch OpenMW and configure the mod from the in-game Settings menu.[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Report a problem[/b][/size]

If you find an issue or have a question, please [url=https://github.com/voshond/openmw-quick-select/issues]open an issue on GitHub[/url].
